UID:52XkCtabdX
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 125 mins (2h05m)\n\nA winner of this year’s Cannes
  Competition Jury Prize\, Sirât is at once a visceral and metaphysical ex
 cursion\, in which a man desperately searches for his missing daughter ami
 d a roving raver.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/sirat\n\nEsti
 mated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Cutoff
DTSTART:20260321T200000Z
DTEND:20260321T214500Z
DTSTAMP:20260321T200000Z
UID:2iLF6Smtpd
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nPresented by Aravaipa Running Th
 e Cutoff is a feature-length documentary set inside Cocodona 250\, a 250 m
 ile ultramarathon across Arizona. This time Dylan Harris followed the unde
 rdogs\, the back of the pack runners who are barely making cutoffs. Who wi
 ll make it and who won't.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/the-c
 utoff-presented-by-aravaipa-running\n\nEstimated start: 13:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tow
DTSTART:20260326T020000Z
DTEND:20260326T041000Z
DTSTAMP:20260326T020000Z
UID:Gs9AKX5WTv
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 115 mins (1h55m)\n\nRose Byrne delivers an unstoppab
 le performance as real-life unhoused hero\, Seattle-ite Amanda Ogle\, whos
 e fight to regain custody of her live-in automobile becomes an unforgettab
 le rallying cry for the little guy.  Q&A with the film team on Friday\, M
 arch 20\, following the 7pm screening. Guests include Producer Brent Stief
 el\, and real-life subjects Amanda and Avery Ogle\, and lawyer Kevin Egger
 s.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/tow\n\nEstimated start: 19:1
 5
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
